cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "FlockWorld: A Multi-Agent World Model of an Egocentric Flocking Simulation"
abstract: >-
  A multi-agent world model of an egocentric flocking simulation: a
  flow-matching transformer that predicts, in the latent space of a small causal
  video autoencoder, the futures of ten agent-centered views of a shared arena,
  conditioned on the agents' accelerations. Includes the simulation environment,
  the model, and a metric suite separating per-view fidelity from
  ground-truth-free cross-view consistency.
authors:
  - name: "Authors to be listed on publication"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wangyz1999/flockworld"
